  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_024: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. We have strong evidence that scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n2000 (~4% gain) and that transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool (~3.5% gain), but we have zero evidence about scgpt as an RNA encoder. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 when paired with the best-known image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), and fusion (weighted)? This is a clean single-variable swap (RNA encoder only) against config_024, isolating the representation choice. Why best next experiment: RNA encoder is the most impactful design axis identified so far, and scgpt is a fundamentally different learned representation (generative vs. variational) that could capture complementary biological structure. Testing it at the current best settings tells us whether to invest further in the scgpt family or commit to scvi_n200, reducing uncertainty on a high-leverage decision with one experiment."
}

